# scripts/.banned — local-only banned-string list for secret-scan.sh (layer 1).
#
# These patterns ARE the secrets (real product names, hostnames, IPs, tokens, ids),
# so the real file must NEVER be committed. Copy this template to scripts/.banned
# (which is gitignored) and fill it with your own infra identifiers — ONE extended
# regular-expression (ERE) per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored; the
# lines are joined with '|' into a single ERE.
#
# For CI, set the SAME patterns as the SECRET_SCAN_BANNED repo secret instead
# (pipe-joined, e.g. "foo|bar\.example\.com|[0-9a-f]{16}"); the workflow passes it
# via env. With neither scripts/.banned nor SECRET_SCAN_BANNED present, layer 1 is
# skipped and only the generic-credential layer (2) runs.
#
#   cp scripts/.banned.example scripts/.banned   # then edit scripts/.banned
#
# --- examples (PLACEHOLDERS — replace with your own; do not commit the real file) ---
# mycompanyname
# myproductname
# subs\.example\.com
# 203\.0\.113\.[0-9]+          # a server IP / range (TEST-NET shown here)
# [0-9a-f]{16}                 # a known API / subscription token shape
